WEBVTT

00:08:58.984 --> 00:09:01.901
Sequence is a very important
aspect of comics.

00:09:02.652 --> 00:09:04.763
Comics presents a kind of temporal map.

00:09:05.946 --> 00:09:09.582
And this temporal map was something
that energizes modern comics,

00:09:09.606 --> 00:09:12.527
but I was wondering
if perhaps it also energizes

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.069
other sorts of forms,

00:09:14.093 --> 00:09:15.525
and I found some in history.

00:09:16.606 --> 00:09:19.290
You can see this same principle operating

00:09:19.314 --> 00:09:22.298
in these ancient versions
of the same idea.

00:09:22.322 --> 00:09:23.475
What's happening is,

00:09:23.499 --> 00:09:25.841
an art form is colliding
with a given technology,

00:09:25.865 --> 00:09:27.206
whether it's paint on stone,

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.627
like the Tomb of Menna the Scribe
in ancient Egypt,

00:09:29.651 --> 00:09:32.255
or a bas-relief sculpture
rising up a stone column,